Backport of qtsvg commit ea44b50c6e61 (QTBUG-137553, "Replace check for endless
recursion when loading") to Qt 6.8.3, for the WebAssembly build only.

Qt 6.8.3 checks the whole SVG tree for reference cycles after every start tag,
which makes loading an SVG quadratic in its number of elements. In the browser
this made part search take about 27 s for 115 results. The fix is in Qt 6.9.3
and 6.8.5; the prebuilt Qt 6.8.3 for wasm_singlethread does not have it.
Upstream: https://github.com/qt/qtsvg/commit/ea44b50c6e61 (test change left out)

diff --git a/src/svg/qsvghandler.cpp b/src/svg/qsvghandler.cpp
index 48f9f0b2..c871a20c 100644
--- a/src/svg/qsvghandler.cpp
+++ b/src/svg/qsvghandler.cpp
@@ -4647,8 +4647,7 @@ void QSvgHandler::parse()
             // this point is to do what everyone else seems to do and
             // ignore the reported namespaceUri completely.
             if (remainingUnfinishedElements
-                    && startElement(xml->name().toString(), xml->attributes())
-                    && !detectCyclesAndWarn(m_doc)) {
+                    && startElement(xml->name().toString(), xml->attributes())) {
                 --remainingUnfinishedElements;
             } else {
                 delete m_doc;
diff --git a/src/svg/qsvgstructure.cpp b/src/svg/qsvgstructure.cpp
